From: Orion <orionopenwow@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] openvanilla: Alt+Enter toggles full screen

As Alt+Enter toggled the window in the 1.12 client. The key press is a user gesture, so the play
page's "full screen" button handler may ask the browser for it; captured ahead of the game, which
would read the Enter as "open the chat box". A loading tip says so (a player asked for full
screen, 2026-10-21, not having seen the small link at the top).

diff --git a/crates/benilla-app/src/game_tip.rs b/crates/benilla-app/src/game_tip.rs
index 41398199..fae89486 100644
--- a/crates/benilla-app/src/game_tip.rs
+++ b/crates/benilla-app/src/game_tip.rs
@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ const OW_TIP_FONT_FRACTION: f32 = 0.0155;
 /// the `GameTips.dbc` rows (gold "Tip:" prefix).
 const OW_TIPS: &[&str] = &[
     "Open Vanilla runs in your browser. The game data you download is kept, so your next visit loads faster.",
-    "The menu at the top of the screen has full screen, notifications and lighter textures for slow connections.",
+    "Alt+Enter plays in full screen. The menu at the top of the screen has it too, with notifications and lighter textures for slow connections.",
     "Lite textures download about a quarter of the texture data. Turn them on from the menu at the top of the screen.",
     "Turn on notifications from the menu to hear about whispers, invites and mail while the game tab is in the background.",
     "In full screen the game keeps Esc, Tab and Ctrl+W. Press and hold Esc to leave full screen.",
diff --git a/crates/wenilla-realm/templates/play.html b/crates/wenilla-realm/templates/play.html
index 32618d05..396521c6 100644
--- a/crates/wenilla-realm/templates/play.html
+++ b/crates/wenilla-realm/templates/play.html
@@ -269,6 +269,16 @@
       installFullscreenToggle(document.getElementById('fs'), {
         focusTarget: document.getElementById('benilla'),
       });
+      // Open Vanilla: Alt+Enter toggles full screen, as it toggled the window in the 1.12 client.
+      // A key press is a user gesture, so the button's own handler may ask the browser for it.
+      // Captured ahead of the game, which would otherwise read the Enter as "open the chat box".
+      const fs = document.getElementById('fs');
+      window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
+        if (!e.altKey || e.key !== 'Enter' || e.repeat || !fs || fs.hidden) return;
+        e.preventDefault();
+        e.stopImmediatePropagation();
+        fs.click();
+      }, { capture: true });
     })
     .catch((e) => console.warn('platform.js:', e));
   // The JavaScript bridge (web/bridge.js, `window.wenilla` in the console): live game state
